{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow\/style\/combined"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","title":"MXLArrow.Style.combined","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLArrowV5StyleO8combinedyA2EmF","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"combined","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style\/combined"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"combined","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"An arrow in one direction combined with an arrow in the other direction.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArrow/Style/combined":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow\/style\/combined","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style\/combined","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"combined","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An arrow in one direction combined with an arrow in the other direction.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"MXLArrow.Style.combined"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArrow/Style":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow\/style","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow\/Style","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrow-style type represents the style of an arrow, using Unicode arrow terminology. Filled and hollow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrows indicate polygonal single arrows. Paired arrows are duplicate single arrows in the same direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Combined arrows apply to double direction arrows like left right, indicating that an arrow in one direction"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be combined with an arrow in the other direction."}],"title":"MXLArrow.Style","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArrow":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarrow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArrow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrow element represents an arrow used for a musical technical indication. It can represent both Unicode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and SMuFL arrows. The presence of an arrowhead element indicates that only the arrowhead is displayed, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrow stem. The smufl attribute distinguishes different SMuFL glyphs that have an arrow appearance such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrowBlackUp, guitarStrumUp, or handbellsSwingUp. The specified glyph should match the descriptive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation."}],"title":"MXLArrow","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArrow"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArrow"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}